      "message": "**File:** `util/egis/flasher_logic.cc`\n\nWhen parsing raw command binaries, you combine `header_size` and `wrapped_size.value()`:\n\n```c\n  return header_size + wrapped_size.value();\n\n```\n\nBecause `wrapped_size.value()` is parsed directly from potentially untrusted or corrupted binary input, an exceptionally large value (e.g., `0xFFFFFFFF`) could cause an integer overflow on 32-bit architectures, wrapping around to a small `size_t`. This would bypass subsequent length checks in `ProgramRawCommandPayload`.\n\n**Remediation:** Validate `wrapped_size.value()` against a reasonable upper bound (like `BootromComm::kMaxPayloadSize`) before returning.\n\n\n```c\n  auto wrapped_size \u003d ReadLittleEndian\u003cuint32_t\u003e(\n      fw.subspan(offsetof(BootromComm::SecureCommandShaHeader, payload_len),\n                 sizeof(BootromComm::SecureCommandShaHeader::payload_len)));\n  if (!wrapped_size) return std::unexpected(ParseError::kInvalidPayloadSize);\n\n  // CRITICAL FIX: Prevent integer overflow and enforce hardware limits\n  if (wrapped_size.value() \u003e BootromComm::kMaxPayloadSize) {\n    return std::unexpected(ParseError::kInvalidPayloadSize); \n  }\n\n  return header_size + wrapped_size.value();\n\n```",
